Why the URL is read before `await`: `watchEffect` tracks only the reactive values read **synchronously**. Anything read after the first `await` won't start a new request when it changes.

**Where it breaks and what to add in production:**
- No cache: two components with the same URL make two requests, and coming back to the page refetches everything. TanStack Query for Vue or VueUse `useFetch` solve that.
- No `refetch()` for a "Try again" button and no way to skip the request (`if (!currentUrl) return` for a URL that isn't ready yet).
- Types: `useFetch<User>(...)` with a generic, so `data` is typed.
- `res.json()` on an empty response (204) throws. Check the status or the `content-type`.
- Data from the previous URL stays on the screen while the new one loads. Decide whether to clear it or show it dimmed.

```vue
<script setup>
import { ref, computed } from 'vue';

// picked outcomes: one per match
const picks = ref([
  { matchId: 1, title: 'Spartak – CSKA', outcome: 'W1', odds: 2.1 },
  { matchId: 2, title: 'Zenit – Dynamo', outcome: 'Over 2.5', odds: 1.85 },
]);
// the stake as typed: a string from the input
const stake = ref('100');
// limits from the bookmaker's rules
const MIN_STAKE = 10;
const MAX_STAKE = 100000;

function addPick(pick) {
  // one match, one outcome: drop the old pick of this match and add the new one
  picks.value = picks.value.filter((p) => p.matchId !== pick.matchId).concat(pick);
}

function removePick(matchId) {
  // remove the match from the slip
  picks.value = picks.value.filter((p) => p.matchId !== matchId);
}

// one pick is a single, several is an express
const type = computed(() => (picks.value.length > 1 ? 'Express' : 'Single'));
// express odds = the product of all odds
const totalOdds = computed(() => picks.value.reduce((acc, p) => acc * p.odds, 1));
// the stake as a number; NaN if the input is junk
const stakeNumber = computed(() => Number(stake.value.replace(',', '.')));
// the slip can be placed: there are picks and the stake is within limits
const isValid = computed(
  () => picks.value.length > 0 && stakeNumber.value >= MIN_STAKE && stakeNumber.value <= MAX_STAKE
);
// the potential win, rounded to kopecks
const potentialWin = computed(() =>
  isValid.value ? Math.round(stakeNumber.value * totalOdds.value * 100) / 100 : 0
);
</script>

<template>
  <section class="slip">
    <!-- the type and the number of picks -->
    <h2>{{ type }} · {{ picks.length }}</h2>
    <ul>
      <!-- one row per match -->
      <li v-for="p in picks" :key="p.matchId">
        {{ p.title }}: {{ p.outcome }} <b>{{ p.odds.toFixed(2) }}</b>
        <button :aria-label="`Remove ${p.title}`" @click="removePick(p.matchId)">✕</button>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <!-- for an express show the total odds -->
    <p v-if="picks.length > 1">Total odds: {{ totalOdds.toFixed(2) }}</p>
    <!-- inputmode="decimal": a numeric keyboard on the phone -->
    <input v-model="stake" inputmode="decimal" aria-label="Stake" />
    <!-- say why the stake is wrong -->
    <small v-if="!isValid && picks.length">Stake from {{ MIN_STAKE }} to {{ MAX_STAKE }}</small>
    <p>Potential win: {{ potentialWin.toFixed(2) }} ₽</p>
    <!-- disabled until the slip is valid -->
    <button :disabled="!isValid">Place bet</button>
  </section>
</template>
```

**Where it breaks and what to add in production:**
- **The client only shows numbers.** The server recalculates the odds and the win when the bet is placed; never trust the client's numbers.
- **Odds change** while the slip is open (live matches). They come over a WebSocket: highlight the change and ask to confirm, or have an "accept any odds changes" setting. A market can be **suspended**: such a pick blocks the bet.
- **Money**: floating point (`0.1 + 0.2`). Keep amounts in integer kopecks or use a decimal library, and format with `Intl.NumberFormat`.
- **Limits**: a maximum total odds and a maximum win, a minimum odds per pick in an express, some outcomes can't be combined in one express (correlated markets).
- **Double click** on "Place bet" makes two bets: disable the button while the request is pending and send an idempotency key.
- The slip lives in a store (Pinia) and in `localStorage`, so it survives navigation and reload. Systems (2 of 3) are a separate calculation: every combination of the picks.

```js
import { ref, computed, watch, nextTick } from 'vue';

async function demo() {
  const count = ref(0);
  // computed: runs only when read, then caches
  const double = computed(() => {
    console.log('computed');
    return count.value * 2;
  });
  // watch: called asynchronously, once per batch of changes
  watch(count, (value) => console.log('watch', value));

  // two changes in a row: the watcher isn't called yet
  count.value = 1;
  count.value = 2;
  // reading computed: it runs now, with the latest value
  console.log('sync', double.value);
  // nothing changed since: the cached value, no 'computed' log
  console.log('again', double.value);
  // wait for Vue's update: the watcher fires here, once, with 2
  await nextTick();
  console.log('after tick');
}
demo();

// computed
// sync 4
// again 4
// watch 2
// after tick
```

